Dragon Rebellion:
The '''Dragon Rebellion''' is an event that took place in [[Ashenfall]] during the end of [[Third Age]] of [[Gielinor]]. It started shortly after the [[Human-Garou War|war]] between the [[Garou (race)|garou]]s and the humans, with the creation of [[Kuldra]]. The dragons were returned to their chains by their masters, the [[Dragonkin (race)|dragonkin]], after assisting [[Lougrim]] and the garou in their war. With the dragons returned to chains they were forced to work in repairing damaged fortresses. Kuldra would witness this and start recruiting not only her own children, but other dragons. One of these dragons, [[Velgar]] would eagerly accept Kuldra's scheme without hesitation, being the first to join her war.{{CiteJournal|journal=Velgar|quote=It is perhaps not wonder, therefore, that he accepted Kuldra's scheme without hesitation. The first to join her war, aside from her own child.}} 

As the war commenced, [[Brakka]] was amongst the dragonkin killed by Kuldra, who devoured him  and shared his essence with Velgar.{{CiteJournal|journal=Fractured Cape|quote=Kuldra, the godeater, crushed him beneath her great claw and feasted on his anima-rich soul. Stealing Brakka’s power for herself. She gifted Velgar, her most trusted general, with the elemental mastery of the fallen Nodon architect.}} Her gaze then turned to Lougrim, in a battle fractured the continent itself{{CiteText|text=Leathery Parchment|quote=The battle was swift and bloody; their clashing energies created cracks in the very earth. The entire continent buckled beneath their fury, but only one of them could prevail.}}, Kuldra fought and killed Lougrim, devouring her body and taking her title of High Queen of the Garou. Having freed her fellow dragons, she sent them out across the continent to wipe out the human settlements.

