'''Durability''' is a property of equippable items in ''RuneScape: Dragonwilds'' - the durability of [[tools]], [[weapons]], [[armour]], and [[shields]] will decrease as they are used in combat. There is no loss of effectiveness associated with loss of durability, but an object will break when it reaches zero. Durability can be repaired either at the facility where the object was made, such as a [[smithing anvil]] or [[crafting table]], or by the use of the [[Magical Mending]] spell. It should be noted that repairing at a facility requires raw materials, while the Magical Mending spell consumes only [[runes]], and as such is likely to be the economical option. However, Magical Mending will only restore half of the tool's maximum durability. For example, if a [[Logging Axes|logging axe]] is at 234/1200, using Magical Mending on the item will add 600, leaving the durability at 834/1200.  

