'''Garou chit''' are currency used by the Moon [[Garou (race)|Garou]] in [[Umbral Sands]].

==Item sources==
Garou chit can be found inside [[Chest (Umbral Sands)|chests]] within the [[Umbral Sands]] region as well as from selling items to a garou merchant. Only a few items can be sold for chit, and the three available merchants have separate lists for what they will purchase from the player.
{{Drop sources list}}

==Strategy==
When starting off, players can obtain a substantial amount of chits by completing the various side quests unlocked during the [[Umbral Sands]] main quest, ''[[Icthlarin's Little Helper]]''.

An efficient way to farm garou chit '''after unlocking''' the appropriate merchants is to sell surplus materials with limited utility at this point in the player's progression, such as [[maple logs]] and [[coarse animal fur]]. 

One of the most effective materials to sell is leather from dragons, as they have no further use beyond the few weapons and armour made from them: Each of the 5 [[green dragon]]s drop 6-8 [[green dragon hide]] which can be processed into 12-16 [[green dragonhide leather]] worth 100 '''garou chit''' each, the 3 [[blue dragon]]s drop 6-8 [[blue dragon hide]] which can be processed into 12-16 [[blue dragon leather]] worth 120 '''garou chit''' each, and the 5(ish) [[red dragon]]s drop 6-8 [[red dragon hide]] which can be processed into 12-16 [[red dragonhide leather]] worth 140 '''garou chit''' each!

That's 18,720 to 24,960 '''garou chit''' for farming all of them, which can easily be done in a day, and once every four or five days! While farming for dragon's rare drops like the [[amulet of glory]], this can be a substantial source of garou chit in the meantime. That's not to mention the [[dragon tooth|dragon teeth]] and [[dragon blood]] as well as other drops that can also be used in other recipes or valuable items, such as [[cooling ferocious infusion]] and [[draconic leather]].

[[File:Kalphite lair eggs.png|thumb|Location of the north-western kalphite egg spawns in the Umbral Sands.]]Another efficient method involves completely clearing the north-westernmost area of the desert of [[kalphite egg]]s to harvest [[kalphite ichor]]s. Clearing the entire zone, including the cave leading to the nearby [[kalphite queen]], yields approximately 800 ichor, which can be sold to [[Iasadair - The Merchant|Iasadair]] for roughly 12,000 garou chit. Using a fast weapon such as [[keris]] or a hard-hitting crush weapon like an [[adamant warhammer]] or [[Adamant Mace|mace]], together with an [[Enchant Weapon: Air|air enchantment]] speeds up the process considerably. The whole process takes about 20 minutes and can be done every day as the eggs respawn daily.

An additional way to farm garou chit for free is to purchase dragonwolf hide from [[Iasadair - The Merchant]] for 45 chit and make it into draconic leather and sell it back for 60 chit. This is also a decent way to gain Artisan experience.

